{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"The Fish: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja34'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 34 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Kulāvakavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Nests </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>4. Macchajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Fish: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Na maṁ sītaṁ na maṁ uṇhaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>It’s not the cold or heat for me, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>na maṁ jālasmi bādhanaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>nor the being caught in the net; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yañca maṁ maññate macchī, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>it’s that my lady, the fish, thinks of me, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>aññaṁ so ratiyā gato”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“He went for joy to another.” </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Macchajātakaṁ catutthaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
